   "Halcyon-researcher": "collaborating",
   "Halcyon-drafter": "accommodating",
   "Halcyon-negotiator": "accommodating"
  },
  "section_notes": "The final rules set a staged 5% then 2% failure limit at 55 °C, which Northwind's 6.2% exceeds and will need to correct, and the remote shut-off mandate with a 5-year retrofit favours Halcyon's 81% compliance. Suppression is required only for new units from 36 months, which lowers Northwind's cost burden relative to Halcyon, while incident reporting is strict but the recall trigger relies on manufacturer or regulator determination."
